\begin{abstract}
This paper introduces the ``Contortionist Turn,''  a digital humanities and materialist intervention that deconstructs the historical extraction, sanitization, and flattening of volatile, subaltern physical technologies into the passive frameworks of orthodox yoga. While mainstream scholarship frequently treats early somatic practices as products of elite Brahmanical quietism, our parallel-core text-mining pipeline scans 20,529 text nodes across the GRETIL and DCS repositories to read these lineages against the grain of orthodox theology. By computing localized sliding-window Jaccard coefficients ($J_{\text{slide}}$ within an inclusive 300-word context envelope), we expose a hyper-dense statistical polarization. Marginalized and outcaste technical guilds -- specifically the \textit{Kir\={a}ta} ($J_{\text{slide}} = 0.9500; N=120$), \textit{Pulinda} ($J_{\text{slide}} = 1.0000; N=28$), \textit{Pulka\'sa} ($J_{\text{slide}} = 1.0000; N=25$), and bamboo-working \textit{Vai\d{n}a} ($J_{\text{slide}} = 0.9375; N=64$) -- cluster with near-absolute concentration within active combat, contortion, and stealth matrices (\texttt{acrobatic\_sorcery}). 

Qualitative cross-validation isolates these exact interfaces within the late-Vedic subversion logs of the \textit{Pa\~{n}cavi\d{m}\'sabr\={a}hma\d{n}a}, the tactical intelligence matrices of the \textit{Artha\'s\={a}stra}, and the physical conditioning descriptions of the \textit{Har\d{s}acarita}. Crucially, we deploy this validated lexicon to execute a ``reverse-capture'' mapping across late-medieval ha\d{t}ha manuals (the \textit{Ha\d{t}haprad\={i}pik\={a}}, \textit{Ghera\d{n}\d{d}asa\d{m}hit\={a}}, and \textit{\'{S}ivasa\d{m}hit\={a}}), exposing a stark, zero-floor distribution pattern for tribal descriptors ($N=0$) standing in direct opposition to hyper-dense clusters for somatic locks ($N=142$) and toxicological variables. This structural asymmetry provides definitive quantitative proof of an ideological extraction heist: elite text-composers systematically vampirized the high-stakes, environmental survival assets and mechanical rigging systems engineered by peripheral guilds, turning them inward as tools for disembodied liberation while permanently erasing the names of their subaltern creators.
\end{abstract}

\textbf{Keywords}: Acro-Yoga Complex, Contortionist Turn, Text-Mining, Longitudinal Methodology, Subaltern, Espionage, Envenomation


